    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adversĭtas</span></b> ,
		ātis, f.
		adversus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>opposition</i>, <i>contrariety.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magnam adversitatem scorpionibus et
					stellionibus putant esse,</span>”
				<i>a great natural hostility</i>, <i>antipathy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 25, 30, § 90</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., <i>misfortune</i>, <i>suffering</i>, Cassiod.</div>
